> Inspect every fixture input and head objective partial

The original diagnostic objective sums f(x)²−log(f'(x)) plus.3 times the
corresponding inverse expression, using the **same supplied x** for both maps.
This is separate from the fitted Gaussian NLL. Each repeated head row remains
an independent set of 11 variables, so the source stores272 input partials and
272×11 head partials,3,264 values in total. The full program retains them all.

The heatmap divides each feature by its own maximum absolute partial, reported
below. Blue denotes−1, white0 and red+1; colour compares normalized signs and
locations, while the table supplies the raw scale. Horizontal positions retain
original fixture-row order. Vertical feature order runs bottom to top: input,
four width logits, four height logits, then three interior-derivative logits.
Exact knots follow the source's right-bin branch. Independent finite differences
check3,192 entries away from six exact-knot rows; all 3,264 stored branch-selected
partials, including knots, are independently compared with explicit local
NumPy differential arithmetic. First derivatives at knots/tails are checked
separately because log-derivative partials can have one-sided jumps.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spline_fixture_gradients.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> f;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/spline_density/spline_fixtures.npz"))f[k]=n::cast(x,n::DType::Float64);
 auto raw=n::concat({f.at("input_gradient"),f.at("head_gradient")},1);
 auto maxima=n::max(n::abs(raw),{0},true);auto normalized=raw/n::where(n::greater(maxima,0.),maxima,n::ones_like(maxima));
 auto flat=normalized.to_vector<double>();std::vector<std::vector<double>> z(272,std::vector<double>(12));
 for(int row=0;row<272;++row)for(int feature=0;feature<12;++feature)z[row][feature]=flat[row*12+feature];
 std::vector<std::string> labels{"input","w0","w1","w2","w3","h0","h1","h2","h3","d1","d2","d3"};
 dm::graphics::RPlot::create().image(n::arange(0,272).to_vector<double>(),n::arange(0,12).to_vector<double>(),z,dm::graphics::diverging_colors(33),-1,1)
 .size(1100,750).margins(98,24,70,84).x_limits(-.5,271.5).y_limits(-.5,11.5)
 .y_ticks(n::arange(0,12).to_vector<double>(),labels).x_label("Original fixture row index").y_label("Input or raw head feature")
 .title("Every fixture partial, normalized by its feature maximum").save_svg("build/spline_fixture_gradients.svg");
 n::save_npz("build/spline_gradient_plot_values.npz",{{"raw",raw},{"column_max_absolute",maxima},{"normalized",normalized}});
 auto maximum=maxima.to_vector<double>();std::print("| Fixture feature | Maximum absolute source partial |\n|---|---:|\n");
 for(int feature=0;feature<12;++feature)std::print("|{}|{:.10f}|\n",labels[feature],maximum[feature]);
}
