> Check actual forward and inverse determinants along their own paths

Reverse-mode differentiation of each output coordinate yields two actual
Jacobian rows. Their positive determinant agrees with the per-row analytic
logdet on all 128 held-out points and all 1,024 inverse samples. The forward
logdet ranges from −.902685165 to .795060277; it is not a global constant.
The inverse logdet is computed from its supplied latent coordinates along the
reversed spline path. The following residual plot retains all 1,152 values,
subtracts the matching analytic value for each row and scales by 1e7 to reveal
Float32 errors. The two row indices refer to different pools, not paired points.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spline_jacobians.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> v,o,samples;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/spline_density/plot_values.npz"))v[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/spline_density/outputs.npz"))o[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/spline_density/samples.npz"))samples[k]=x;
 auto a=(v.at("actual_logdet")-n::cast(o.at("forward_logdet"),n::DType::Float64))*1e7,b=(v.at("inverse_actual_logdet")-n::cast(samples.at("inverse_logdet"),n::DType::Float64))*1e7;
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points(n::arange(0,128).to_vector<double>(),a.to_vector<double>(),"Forward, all128 test rows",{37,99,235},3)
 .points(n::arange(0,1024).to_vector<double>(),b.to_vector<double>(),"Inverse, all1024 prior rows",{234,88,12},2)
 .y_limits(-8,10).x_label("Row index in its own pool").y_label("(Actual - analytic logdet) x 1e7")
 .title("Actual Jacobians match each per-point log determinant")
 .save_svg("build/spline_jacobians.svg");
}
```
